* FD-05  Output swing (DC)
* Spec 3.1.2.1, Fig. 28: R1 = R3 = {{R_HALF}} ohm, R2 = R4 = {{R_NET}} ohm (R1 <= R2,
* gain -2), VIN on R1, VCOM on R3; VIN swept 0 .. VDD in 2 mV steps.  The
* linear range is where |dVod/dVin| stays >= 90 % of its value at VCOM; the
* bench reports the differential range and each output's single-ended range.
{{SEED_OPTION}}
.lib "{{MODEL_LIB}}" {{CORNER}}
{{MC_PARAM}}
.include "{{DUT_FILE}}"
.temp {{TEMP}}
.options reltol=1e-6 abstol=1e-15 vntol=1e-9
VDD vdd 0 {{VDD}}
VSS vss 0 0
IBIAS vdd ibias {{IBIAS}}
VCM vcm 0 {{VCM}}
VI vi 0 {{VCM}}
R1 vi inp {{R_HALF}}
R2 inp outn {{R_NET}}
R3 vcm inn {{R_HALF}}
R4 inn outp {{R_NET}}
XDUT vss ibias vdd vcmpin inp inn outp outn {{DUT}}
RVCM_DUT vcm vcmpin 1k
RLP outp vcm {{RL}}
CLP outp 0 {{CL}}
RLN outn vcm {{RL}}
CLN outn 0 {{CL}}
.control
set filetype=ascii
dc vi 0 {{VDD}} 0.002
write {{RAW}} v(outp) v(outn)
.endc
.end
